            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A retinal disease that is characterized by increased sensitivity to blue light; perception of blue light is mediated by what is normally the least populous cone photoreceptor subtype, the S (short wavelength, blue) cones and suffer visual loss, with night blindness occurring from early in life, varying degrees of L (long, red)- and M (middle, green)-cone vision, and retinal degeneration that has_material_basis_in homozygous or compound heterozygous mutation in the nuclear receptor gene NR2E3 on chromosome 15q23.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MIM:268100</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>disease_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>DOID:0061231</oboInOwl:id>
