            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 1 characterized by delayed motor development in the first years of life associated with gait abnormalities, sensory ataxia, hyporeflexia, and distal sensory impairment due to a sensorimotor peripheral neuropathy that mainly affects the lower limbs that has_material_basis_in heterozygous mutation in the POLR3B gene on chromosome 12q23. This disease is progressive.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MIM:619742</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
