        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">A commensal Clostridium infectious disease that is caused by ingestion of food contaminated with Clostridium perfringens, which produces an enterotoxin that acts on the small intestine. The symptoms include watery diarrhea, abdominal cramps, a severe decrease in blood pressure and abdominal expansion from gas.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:type rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECO_0007637"/>
