        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">A viral infectious disease that results_in infection, has_material_basis_in Colorado tick fever virus (Coltivirus dermacentoris), which is transmitted_by rocky mountain wood tick, Dermacentor andersoni. The infection has_symptom fever for 2-3 days, followed by an afebrile period of similar duration and then another 2-3 days of fever, has_symptom headache, has_symptom myalgia, and has_symptom fatigue.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:type rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECO_0007637"/>
