        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">A viral infectious disease that is a hemorrhagic fever, has_material_basis_in Omsk hemorrhagic fever virus (Orthoflavivirus omskense), which is transmitted_by Dermacentor and transmitted_by Ixodes species of ticks. The infection has_symptom fever, has_symptom chills, has_symptom headache, has_symptom pain in lower and upper extremities, has_symptom stiff neck, has_symptom papulovesicular rash on the soft palate, has_symptom cervical lymphadenopathy, has_symptom conjunctival suffusion, has_symptom blood in the urine, and has_symptom blood in the sputum.</owl:annotatedTarget>
