        <obo:IAO_0000115>A  balance symptom that is characterized by a condition of being dizzy or on the verge of fainting, particularly when one arises to a standing position. Lightheadedness is a predictable consequence of any medication tending to lower blood pressure.</obo:IAO_0000115>
